<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 3.18bln rupees bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 3.18bln rupees bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned federal bonds worth 3.18 billion rupees in an open market operation on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said bids worth 2.18 billion rupees were accepted for outright sale of six-month bonds at a maximum cut-off of 17.25 percent while bids worth one billion rupees were accepted for five-month repos at a maximum cut-off of 17 percent.</p>
<p>In the previous such operation held on December 18, bids worth 1.055 billion rupees were accepted for the outright sale of the six-month bonds at a maximum cut-off of 16.75 percent per annum. -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
